+// AdmitFrom makes the manager refuse any app that has not been onboarded to the environment its
+// change lands in.
+//
+// Optional at wiring time and NOT at decision time. Without a store nothing is consulted and
+// Apply behaves exactly as it did before this existed, because making a released module refuse
+// every app until a new collaborator is supplied is an outage delivered as a minor version. With
+// a store, every unconfirmed app is refused — including when the store cannot be reached.
+//
+// A deployment that wires none must say so out loud at boot, the way it does for
+// [MemoryApprovals]: an operator must never discover which controls are running from behaviour.
+func (m *Manager) AdmitFrom(admissions Admissions) *Manager {
+	m.admissions = admissions
+	return m
+}
